      "conditions": [],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 826,
          "quote": "Only\n`satisfied` establishes the predicate. `falsified` establishes that the\npredicate fails and names the counterexample. `indeterminate`,\n`out_of_frame` and `invalid_basis` establish neither, and each names what\nwould decide: the evidence, the missing relation or capability with its\nowner where the subject gives one, or the basis repair. By support for the\npredicate, `satisfied` stands above each other value, and the other four\nare not ordered among themselves.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults",
          "start_line": 819
        },
        {
          "end_line": 816,
          "quote": "A mapping into the core never owns domain\nmeaning: the member, profile or adopting Product that defines the refined\nvalue keeps it, and a consumer that needs the domain distinction reads the\ndomain outcome, never the core value alone (P1, P6).",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults",
          "start_line": 813
        }
      ],
      "key": "recording_and_standing",
      "statement": "Record core value, evaluated predicate and original domain outcome; its definer retains domain meaning, and consumers needing that distinction read the domain outcome. Only satisfied establishes the predicate; falsified establishes failure and names its counterexample. Indeterminate, out_of_frame and invalid_basis establish neither truth nor failure and name respectively deciding evidence, missing relation/capability with owner where supplied, or basis repair. Satisfied stands above each other value by predicate support; the other four have no intrinsic ordering.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["evaluation_result", "result_refinement"],
      "conditions": [],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 838,
          "quote": "No refinement or mapping raises a result's standing (P5, P6):\n\n- a falsified or failed result never maps to a satisfied or successful one;\n- a result that admissible evidence cannot decide never maps to\n  `satisfied`;\n- an evaluation that was not performed stays distinct from one whose\n  evidence cannot decide: it has no\n  [closed result](ACTIVATION.md#7-closed-result-and-reuse), and it is never mapped\n  to `indeterminate` or to any other core value;\n- an effect whose completion is unknown never maps to no effect or to\n  completed.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults",
